Question: Find the destination airports that receive flights from both 'SFO' and 'ORD'.
Target SQL: SELECT destairport FROM flights WHERE sourceairport = 'SFO' INTERSECT SELECT destairport FROM flights WHERE sourceairport = 'ORD'

Database: flight_2
Schema:
CREATE TABLE airports (city text, airportcode text PRIMARY KEY, airportname text, country text, countryabbrev text);
CREATE TABLE airlines (airlineid int PRIMARY KEY, airlinename text, abbreviation text, country text);
CREATE TABLE flights (airline int, flightno int, sourceairport text, destairport text, PRIMARY KEY (airline, flightno));
Question: Which airline has the highest number of flights connecting international airports outside their home country?
Target SQL: SELECT T1.airlinename FROM airlines AS T1 JOIN flights AS T2 ON T1.airlineid = T2.airline GROUP BY T1.airlinename ORDER BY count(*) DESC LIMIT 1

Database: academic
Schema:
CREATE TABLE author (aid int PRIMARY KEY, name text, oid int);
CREATE TABLE publication (pid int PRIMARY KEY, title text, year int, jid int);
CREATE TABLE writes (aid int, pid int, PRIMARY KEY (aid, pid));
CREATE TABLE domain_author (aid int, did int, PRIMARY KEY (aid, did));
CREATE TABLE domain (did int PRIMARY KEY, name text);
Question: Find papers written by authors who have authored more than 10 papers in year 2021.
Target SQL: SELECT T1.title FROM publication AS T1 JOIN writes AS T2 ON T1.pid = T2.pid WHERE T1.year = 2021 GROUP BY T1.title HAVING count(T2.aid) > 10
